    "title": "What should SNAP recipients do with spoiled food from power outage? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "(WHTM) — Spoiled food is piling up as thousands in central Pennsylvania continue without power. For people receiving SNAP benefits, formerly known as food stamps, this can make for an especially devastating loss. However, the Pennsylvania Department of Human Services said there’s help available. The law allows SNAP benefit replacements for food lost during a power outage, fire or other household misfortunes, the department said. This covers up to one month’s benefits. Those looking to get replacement benefits should: For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJET/WFXP/YourErie.com.",
